# Citation metadata of OpenSPS (https://citation-file-format.github.io). The FSPS papers are
# listed under references: please cite them in any work that uses this library.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OpenSPS in your research, please cite it using this metadata,
  and also cite the FSPS papers listed under references (Conroy, Gunn & White
  2009; Conroy & Gunn 2010).
title: "OpenSPS"
abstract: >-
  A high-performance, hardware-accelerated stellar population synthesis
  library. OpenSPS is derived from FSPS (Flexible Stellar Population
  Synthesis) by Charlie Conroy and contributors: a thread-safe Fortran 2008
  code with a stable C API, batched composite populations for fitting, FP32
  kernels and GPU offload.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/elijahmathews/libopensps"
url: "https://github.com/elijahmathews/libopensps"
keywords:
  - stellar population synthesis
  - galaxies
  - spectral energy distributions
  - astronomy
authors:
  - family-names: Mathews
    given-names: Elijah P.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0384-0681"
    email: pgp@elijahmathews.com
    affiliation: "The Pennsylvania State University"
# version must equal the project version in meson.build (tools/check_versions.py, run by CI and
# the release workflow, fails otherwise). date-released is left out: GitHub and Zenodo take the
# release date from the release itself. Add the archive DOI once there is one.
version: "0.2.1"
# doi: "10.5281/zenodo.TODO"
